  m_Name: Emerald Ash Borer
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  bugName: Emerald Ash Borer
  info: "The Emerald Ash Borer is a green beetle native to north-eastern Asia that
    feeds on ash trees.\n\n Females lay their eggs on the bark of the host tree and
    the larvae burrow under the bark and feed on the tree for one to two years before
    emerging as adults. \n\nOutside of its native range the beetle is an invasive
    species that is highly destructive to the ash trees in its introduced range"
  bugImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 94fda7390f458a54f8790f65e25f349b, type: 3}
